<title>NORWAY: NORDIC SKIING-PROFILE OF MEN'S 50-KM WINNER.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-PROFILE OF MEN'S 50-KM WINNER.</headline>
<dateline>TRONDHEIM, Norway 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profile of the winner of Sunday's men's 50-km, classical style cross-country race at the Nordic skiing world championships:</p>
<p>Name: Mika Myllylae</p>
<p>Age: 27</p>
<p>Country: Finland</p>
<p>Previous world titles: none</p>
<p>Other facts: The porwerful Myllylae, who posted two wins on the World Cup circuit this winter, had already taken three medals in the Trondheim championships with silver in the 15-km pursuit and the relay and bronze in the 10-km classic.</p>
</text>
